at system of highways that tied together the provinces of the Classic Khmer Empire has hardly begun.\' \'[Jayavarman VII] saw to the construction of many other buildings across his empire, including roads with guesthouses every 9.3 miles (15 km) that linked Angkor with viceregal centers such as Phimai.\' \'Highways were built—straight, stone-paved roads running across hundreds of kilometers, raised above the flood level, with stone bridges across rivers and lined with rest houses every 15 kilometers.\' \'In the 1200s, if not earlier, a system of raised highways linked Angkor to Phimai and other key towns.\''}], {'usage.total_tokens': 944, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 866})
